**Issue 6 — `[P2] (confidence: 9/10)` selection has the same two-homes problem you just resolved for frames.**

`WindowSession.selectedTargetID` duplicates a value that already persists, gated to one window:

```swift
// AppStore.swift:161-165
@Published var selectedTargetID: SidebarID? {
  didSet {
    if persistsSidebarPrefs {
      Defaults[.sidebarSelection] = Self.targetIDString(for: selectedTargetID)
    }
```

With N restored windows each carrying its own selection in the session file, `Defaults[.sidebarSelection]` becomes a single-slot shadow of an N-slot value — written by whichever window was last key, read on restore only as a fallback.

