/// The pane's content for a saved session: the scrollback, then what is currently on screen.
///
/// **Two reads, deliberately.** `SCREEN` would fetch both in one call, but while a TUI holds the
/// alternate screen it returns the TUI's frame *and* hides the primary history — so quitting with
/// vim open would persist a frozen vim screenshot and lose the real session. `SURFACE` can never
/// return alternate-screen content, so reading it means TUI exclusion needs no code at all: it
/// falls out of the tag choice. `VIEWPORT` then adds the visible lines `SURFACE` omits (and is
/// itself alt-screen content when a TUI is up, which is why it is dropped in that case).
func captureScrollback(maxBytes: Int = SessionLimits.maxScrollbackBytes) -> String? {
  let history = readText(tag: GHOSTTY_POINT_SURFACE)
  // A TUI is on screen exactly when there is no readable history but a viewport exists; in that
  // case the viewport IS the TUI frame, so keep only the history (here, nothing).
  let visible = history == nil ? nil : readText(tag: GHOSTTY_POINT_VIEWPORT)
  let combined = [history, visible].compactMap { $0 }.joined(separator: "\n")
  guard !combined.isEmpty else { return nil }
  return TerminalCapture.tidy(combined, maxBytes: maxBytes)
}

